4.2.m:
Dharmarāja said:
'What merit does he have, O minister? State the essence in my presence;
having heard it thus, I shall arrange where he should be placed.'

That ground became smeared [smooth] and free of holes and cracks.
By the power of that merit, his great sin has gone away;
he is fit for Vaikuṇṭha and is released from your punishment.'

Vyāsa said:
Hearing his word, he gave him a seat made of gold;
and seated there, he was worshipped by Yama.

4.8.m:
Sūta said:
O Brahmin, I shall tell in brief the cause of the churning of the ocean;
hear that legendary history, the dialogue between Durvāsas and Indra.
